# Cloudflare Pages headers — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# Security headers on every response
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Revalidate HTML so a new deploy shows immediately (no stale edge copy)
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# ── THE EXTENSIONLESS CHECKOUT RETURN PATH, DECLARED RATHER THAN INHERITED ───
# `_headers` rules match the REQUEST path, not the file that ends up serving it.
# Every stamped app sends a returning buyer to `https://nikatru.com/checkout-
# return` — no extension (apps/<id>/lib/state/money_providers.dart's
# CHECKOUT_RETURN_URL default, and the brick template it is stamped from) — and
# Cloudflare Pages serves `checkout-return.html` for it. That request path
# matches `/*.html` NOWHERE, so without this line the one URL in the whole money
# flow that a paying stranger lands on would be the only page on this root
# running on a platform default nobody chose. Measured default is the same value
# (see the .css/.js note below, where robots.txt, sitemap.xml and llms.txt all
# returned `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`) — so this changes nothing that
# is served today, which is the same bargain and the same reason as the two
# class rules below: a policy is declared before it is needed, not discovered
# afterwards on the page it was needed for.
/checkout-return
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# ── CSS and JS: DECLARED, not inherited ─────────────────────────────────────
# 🔴 2026-08-04. Until today these two classes had no rule here at all, and
# that was not a decision — it was a gap the Cloudflare zone happened to be
# filling. `nikatru.com`'s Browser Cache TTL was 14400, and Cloudflare
# edge-caches .css and .js by extension, so anything of those types this zone
# served was stamped `max-age=14400` whatever the origin declared. The override
# is now off (the zone is on "Respect Existing Headers"), which fixed a real
# bug on subly.nikatru.com — /flutter_bootstrap.js and /main.dart.js were being
# given a four-hour browser cache against a declared `max-age=0`, so a
# returning visitor ran the PREVIOUS build and reported its version honestly,
# invisible to exactly the force-update kill switch that exists for it. Turning
# it off also left .css and .js here with nothing choosing a policy at all.
#
# MEASURED, not assumed, 2026-08-04:
#   · this site serves NO external CSS or JS today. Every page carries its
#     styles in an inline <style> block, and /assets/tokens.css and
#     /assets/base.css both return 404. (Those files live in
#     sites/_shared/assets/ — the Eleventy layer whose `_site/` output is
#     gitignored and deploys nowhere; see sites/_shared/README.md.)
#   · a path with NO rule here gets the Cloudflare Pages default, which
#     measured as `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` — robots.txt,
#     sitemap.xml and llms.txt all returned it.
#
# So the two rules below change nothing that is served today. THAT IS THE
# POINT: a policy file has to declare the class BEFORE the first file of that
# class exists, because the alternative is that the first stylesheet ships on
# whatever the platform or the zone happens to be defaulting to that week.
#
# WHY REVALIDATE AND NOT `immutable`. The CSS these sites will serve once they
# migrate onto sites/_shared is `tokens.css` and `base.css` — STABLE names with
# CHANGING content. `tokens.css` is GENERATED by Style Dictionary out of
# packages/tokens (it changed today) and `base.css` is hand-edited; neither
# name moves when its bytes do. `immutable` on a stable name means a CSS fix
# never reaches anyone who has already visited — for a year, and without even a
# revalidation on an explicit reload. This takes the same one-round-trip
# bargain apps/subly/web/_headers takes for its entry points.
#
# Declared at ANY DEPTH (`/*.css`, not `/assets/*.css`) on purpose: the gap
# being closed is a file arriving somewhere nobody wrote a rule for, and a
# directory-scoped rule reopens it the moment a stylesheet lands at the root.
#
# ⚠️ NOT the Pages Function. /api/subscribe is served by
# functions/api/subscribe.js as a ROUTE, not as a .js asset, so neither rule
# below touches it.
/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Long-cache immutable static assets — but ONLY names that carry a version.
# `founder-v4.jpg` / `founder-v4.webp` carry theirs IN THE NAME, which is what
# makes `immutable` correct for them: a new cut gets a new name, so no cached
# copy can ever be the wrong one.
#
# 🔴 FIXED 2026-08-21 — `/*.png` NO LONGER SAYS `immutable`. THIS IS THE SECOND
# CORRECTION TO THIS BLOCK IN ONE DAY, and both earlier records are kept below
# rather than deleted: each names a DIFFERENT wrong reason, and the wrong
# reasons are the whole story of why this gap stood as long as it did.
#
# THE FACTS THAT DID NOT CHANGE: `icon-16/32/192/512.png`,
# `apple-touch-icon.png` and `og-image.png` are STABLE names with CHANGING
# content. Nothing in those names moves when their bytes do. Under `immutable`,
# replacing the brand mark under one of them would not reach a returning
# visitor for a year — and not even on an explicit reload, because `immutable`
# suppresses revalidation rather than merely extending freshness.
#
# ── WRONG REASON #1, recorded here until this morning ────────────────────────
# "These are the page's heaviest bytes and re-cutting them is a brand decision,
# so the call is the owner's." Re-cutting the ARTWORK is a brand decision — that
# half was true and still is. But re-cutting was never what this gap needed. Two
# different acts were filed under one owner-gate, and the cheap one inherited
# the expensive one's veto.
#
# ── WRONG REASON #2, recorded here this morning, MEASURED FALSE this afternoon ─
# The morning's correction said the fix was to RENAME the files so the name
# carries a version token (`icon-192-v1.png`), and called that "not a brand act
# at all — its whole cost is a mechanical edit" across the 16 files under
# sites/nikatru/ that name them. THE COUNT WAS RIGHT; THE CONCLUSION WAS WRONG.
# Re-measured 2026-08-21 (main loop), those 16 files are not 16 mechanical edits:
#   · THREE are the DATED LEGAL SNAPSHOTS — legal/2026-07-26/en/privacy.html,
#     legal/2026-08-01/en/privacy.html and legal/2026-08-10/en/privacy.html.
#     Those are FROZEN CONSENT RECORDS: what a user agreed to on that date, kept
#     unedited on purpose, and the DO-NOT list forbids editing them beyond head
#     tags. The same rule is encoded one tree over — check-site-integrity.mjs
#     keeps its link-rewriting limb off them because "rewriting a link inside a
#     published policy archive edits the record". So a rename leaves exactly two
#     outcomes: the icon 404s on three published policy pages, or a consent
#     record is edited to keep a favicon working. Neither is available, and no
#     amount of care makes it available.
#   · TWO are GENERATED — apps/subly.html and apps/index.html, written by
#     tooling/sites/generate-discovery.mjs and diffed in CI.
#   · ONE is apps/_template.html, which no pass here owns.
# THE RENAME IS THEREFORE DEAD, NOT DEFERRED AND NOT OWNER-GATED. Do not
# re-propose it; the blocker is a frozen legal record, which no decision unfreezes.
#
# ── THE FIX THIS FILE WAS ALREADY ARGUING FOR, a few rules above ─────────────
# See "WHY REVALIDATE AND NOT `immutable`" over the .css/.js rules: STABLE names
# with CHANGING content take the one-round-trip revalidating bargain, precisely
# so that a fix reaches someone who has already visited. That is the icons'
# situation exactly — the same sentence, about a different extension. The file
# held the answer the whole time while the png rule sat under a deferral about
# artwork.
#
# 🔴 AND THIS IS WHY IT NEEDED NO OWNER AT ALL: a Cache-Control value is not a
# re-cut and not a rename. It changes not one pixel and not one filename, so
# there is no brand question in it to defer. The owner-gate was real, but it was
# attached to a different act than the one performed here.
#
# THE COST, stated so it is weighed and not discovered later: a returning
# visitor now spends ONE conditional request per icon instead of zero, and the
# bytes still come from the local cache on the 304. That is the identical
# bargain /*.css and /*.js take above, and the one apps/subly/web/_headers takes
# for its entry points.
#
# ⚠️ `og-image.png` IS COVERED BY THIS RULE TOO, and deliberately. A RENAME was
# the one fix that carried a genuine cost for this file — social platforms cache
# the card they scraped from the OLD URL, every link already shared points at
# it, and it would 404 until each platform re-scraped. A header change has no
# such cost: the URL never moves. The expensive fix is not needed for the cheap
# problem.
#
# ⚠️ NOT TOUCHED, and why: /*.jpg, /*.webp and /*.svg keep `immutable`. jpg and
# webp are founder-v4's, whose name carries its version. No .svg is served here
# today, so that line is a class declared before its first file arrives — same
# reasoning as /*.css above. If a STABLE-named .jpg/.webp/.svg ever lands here,
# this same argument applies to it unchanged, and assert-web-cache-policy.mjs
# names such a file on every run rather than failing the build.
#
# Nothing here has gone quiet: that guard still prints every stable name left
# under `immutable`, so the remaining instance of this defect — the identical
# `/*.png` rule on sites/rajasekarselvam, which this pass does not own — stays
# visible on every run instead of becoming permanent by being invisible.
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/site.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
